      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "Sub::HandlesVia for Perl before 0.050002 allows untrusted code from the current working directory ('.') to be loaded similar to CVE-2016-1238.  If an attacker can place a malicious file in current working directory, it may be loaded instead of the intended file, potentially leading to arbitrary code execution.  Sub::HandlesVia uses Mite to produce the affected code section due to CVE-2025-30672",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
